{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1363599-dark-eras-2-hunger-in-the-black-land-middle-kingdom-egypt","id":1363599,"title":"[Dark Eras 2] Hunger in the Black Land - Middle Kingdom Egypt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-27T04:51:32-08:00","id":1363599,"title":"[Dark Eras 2] Hunger in the Black Land - Middle Kingdom Egypt","content":"Did not see the topic for this era - so starting now. \ud83d\ude0e <br /> <br /> I very like that this era can work also as introduction to 2E Mummy: the Curse, when someone is intimidated by the style of original corebook. Also, interesting is focus on beasts, werewolves and Prometheans in those times. <br /> <br /> Good read! More interesting thoughts I will write later. \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T06:20:05-08:00","id":1363610,"title":"","content":"I wonder why in A'stru and Duat frame are only Assessors - but not Judges of Duat? They are both the same beings, only different names, in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T07:34:56-08:00","id":1363624,"title":"","content":"Wyrd, have you read <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/146995/Sothis-Ascends?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Sothis Ascends</a>? There's a couple of shout-outs to it in this chapter and if you want to run a Mummy game here, it might be useful. <br /> <br /> (And also for the record, I didn't write this era so I can't answer questions about it. Just giving some words to the wise)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T22:51:37-08:00","id":1363919,"title":"","content":"Reading more Beast side of era - We see here that future Heroes - now Oracles - are not yet locked in the narrations of Primordial Dream, being more diviners than direct warriors. I wonder WHEN, exactly, this change comes. At time of Egypt's New Kingdom? At the start of Greeks mythos of heroes slaining monsters? What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-01-2020, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T09:24:18-08:00","id":1364174,"title":"","content":"Beast part - Oracles ( then era Heroes ) are mechanically using Presence + Expression to show mortals weakness of the Beast, putting Anathema on Begotten by talking about it to other humans. Should not this be Persuassion roll instead? It's more convincing that 'dance, singing and crafts' roll...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T09:24:54-08:00","id":1364175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1363599-dark-eras-2-hunger-in-the-black-land-middle-kingdom-egypt?p=1363610#post1363610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder why in A'stru and Duat frame are only Assessors - but not Judges of Duat? They are both the same beings, only different names, in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite able to parse what you're asking here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T09:34:53-08:00","id":1364180,"title":"","content":"There is sidebar on the page 23 of <b>Dark Eras</b> 2 -<br /> <br /> <b><i>A\u2019aru, Ma\u2019at, and the Duat</i></b><br /> <i>The people of Kemet believe that, after death, parts of the soul travel west to the Duat, an underworld region where everyone must submit to the verdict of 42 Assessors and Anpu\u2019s test of ma\u2019at. The worthy pass before Wesir, reborn for eternity into the fertile, starry paradise of A\u2019aru where they farm and live in divine prosperity. Wesir throws the unworthy to the jaws of Ammut the devourer, who utterly destroys them.</i><br /> <br /> Should not this mentions that Assessors are called Judges of Duat by the mummies of <b>Mummy: The Curse</b>? As this is crossover era, by being that of <b>Beast: the Primordia</b><b>l</b> one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-01-2020, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T00:50:49-08:00","id":1364296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1363599-dark-eras-2-hunger-in-the-black-land-middle-kingdom-egypt?p=1364180#post1364180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is sidebar on the page 23 of <b>Dark Eras</b> 2 -<br /> <br /> <b><i>A\u2019aru, Ma\u2019at, and the Duat</i></b><br /> <i>The people of Kemet believe that, after death, parts of the soul travel west to the Duat, an underworld<br /> region where everyone must submit to the verdict of 42 Assessors and Anpu\u2019s test of ma\u2019at. The worthy pass<br /> before Wesir, reborn for eternity into the fertile, starry paradise of A\u2019aru where they farm and live in divine<br /> prosperity. Wesir throws the unworthy to the jaws of Ammut the devourer, who utterly destroys them.</i><br /> <br /> Should not this mentions that Assessors are called Judges of Duat by the mummies of <b>Mummy: The Curse</b>? As this is crossover era, by being that of <b>Beast: the Primordia</b>l one?</div> </div> </div> </div>While Beast encourages Crossover, it is still its own gamelines- and the Judges are so BIG in Mummy that outright using their name would shift the focus towards that gameline on the expanse of the core gamelines. Besides, it helps to create the distance between the Judges of Duat and the way the Judges are seen in the eyes of local mythology and religion. Anyone who is familiar with Mummy could easily connect the Assessors to the Judges, and those who are not (or prefer not to) could invent their own way to view them, from the flawed version of the Judges through mortal eyes to some astral, dead or spiritual reflection of those gods. It helps to reinforce a mythic feeling of that Era, IMO, and stops Mummy from overtaking a setting which is not a Mummy setting.<br /> <br /> In short, you have nothing to lose from using different terminology, and everything to gain. Those who know Mummy can connect the dots by themselves, and not everything need to be spelled out- especially in the CofD, where it is not impossible that while the Judges exist, there are other incarnations of them and Duat, created by what people believe the Judges were, or from those beings who tried to style themselves as the Judges for their own reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T05:14:39-08:00","id":1364520,"title":"","content":"I read all era up to end of Beasts part - and I see there is a lot of term <i>isfet</i>, written in lower letters - which I still do not know the meaning off. I know that <i>Ma'at</i> is both goddess and personification of ( Supernatural ) Justice - than written lower case as <i>ma'at</i> means general principles of those in monsters society. <i>Isfet</i>, written in upper case, is also goddess, contrary to Ma'at in her dominion - i.e. Injustice - but I do not understand what means, directly in play, <i>isfet</i> written as such. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, I could not find on modern maps location of Atef-Pehu, but <a href=\"https://assassinscreed.fandom.com/wiki/Atef-Pehu_Nome\" target=\"_blank\">Assasin's Creed wiki helped</a>, somehow, with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-01-2020, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T06:35:00-08:00","id":1364528,"title":"","content":"Isfet is chaos or disorder.<br /> <br /> You wont find Atef-Pehu on modern maps because its the ancient Egyptian name for the place, and modern names are likely to be in Arabic instead. The Arabic name for the area is Faiyum.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T09:59:34-08:00","id":1364554,"title":"","content":"Promethean part reading time - Xibalbans Lineage from Meso-America idea sounds interesting, especially as Galateids predecessor. Somehow a bit weird, as Galateids are about love and Xibalbans are about dying, both on Sanguine Humor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-01-2020, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T12:04:09-08:00","id":1364576,"title":"","content":"The Xibalbans are not about dying as much as they are about sacrifice- and it is not the first time that we see such a difference. The Amirani and the Frankensteins share an humor, but the first is about faith and zeal and the second about fury and pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T14:14:31-08:00","id":1364606,"title":"","content":"Werewolf part of the era - What is <i>saharusum</i>? From contexts I assume it's Packs, but I'm not sure I get it right...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T17:45:59-08:00","id":1364648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1363599-dark-eras-2-hunger-in-the-black-land-middle-kingdom-egypt?p=1364606#post1364606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf part of the era - What is <i>saharusum</i>? From contexts I assume it's Packs, but I'm not sure I get it right...</div> </div> </div> </div>'the saharusum, the children of Crocodile.' 'The saharusum are shapeshifters, also known as the Sobeki.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T22:01:45-08:00","id":1364693,"title":"","content":"Thanks. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>, missed this.<br /> <br /> Divide over Forsaken and Pure Tribes imply that Oaths of the Moon are already set in this era. ( That is circa 1800 BCE. ) This means that in <b><i>Dogs of Sumer</i></b> times Tribes were already a thing - not a Sects of <b><i>Sundered World</i></b>. ( Sumerian civilization is dated 4500 BCE till 1900 BCE, more or less. ) Sad news for your project, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a>?<br /> <br /> I wonder then WHEN Tribes came to being - with <i>Ur-Farah</i> death circa 5000 BCE, they were created and joined in coming 500 years, something like 4500 BCE? Maybe Tribes really did start to crystallize in the start of the Sumer and develop with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-02-2020, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T22:52:00-08:00","id":1364697,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I like the change of name to my favorite Tribe - <i>Iron Masters</i> - to the <i>Watchers Beyond the Flame</i>. I understand that <a href=\"https://www.history.com/topics/pre-history/iron-age\" target=\"_blank\">Iron Age comes between 1200 and 600 BCE</a>, at various places - but the change on the meaning of the Tribe names do not sit well with me. Iron Masters are all about embracing humanity and humans things. 'Beyond the Flame' implies to look <b>outside</b> of humans settlements. I'm not sure here.<br /> <br /> Also, question rise WHEN whole Tribe change the name to modern one, in usage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T00:18:00-08:00","id":1364710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1363599-dark-eras-2-hunger-in-the-black-land-middle-kingdom-egypt?p=1364693#post1364693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>, missed this.<br /> <br /> Divide over Forsaken and Pure Tribes imply that Oaths of the Moon are already set in this era. ( That is circa 1800 BCE. ) This means that in <b><i>Dogs of Sumer</i></b> times Tribes were already a thing - not a Sects of <b><i>Sundered World</i></b>. ( Sumerian civilization is dated 4500 BCE till 1900 BCE, more or less. ) Sad news for your project, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a>?<br /> <br /> I wonder then WHEN Tribes came to being - with <i>Ur-Farah</i> death circa 5000 BCE, they were created and joined in coming 500 years, something like 4500 BCE? Maybe Tribes really did start to crystallize in the start of the Sumer and develop with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>considering the city Bau is based on would set Hunting Grounds Ancient Sumer about a thousand years before Hunger in the Black Land, I\u2019m not seeing a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T02:44:07-08:00","id":1364723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1363599-dark-eras-2-hunger-in-the-black-land-middle-kingdom-egypt?p=1364697#post1364697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Beyond the Flame' implies to look <b>outside</b> of humans settlements. I'm not sure here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know English isn't your strongest point but you're thinking a bit too narrow about this. Seeing beyond a fire could also mean seeing the consequences/effects of fire. Heating, lighting, cooking, even metallurgy which would tie into their future name.<br /> It could also mean that they are watchers that stay outside the reach of a flame's light, watching towards the flame and/or away from it. If the former, then they'd be observing human civilisation and technology. I.e. their favoured hunting grounds, prey, technology, and even territory. If the latter, then they're patrolling and guarding a settlement, which is part of their Tribal Oath.<br /> Or it could be all of these meanings, or it could be for even more symbolic and esoteric reasons that makes the name's meaning hard to guess without enough contextual clues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T05:01:56-08:00","id":1364733,"title":"","content":"Short version; English is a weird language and there are multiple metaphorical meanings that the 'old' name can use to be relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-fa